scenario_text:
**HubSpot CRM — Account: 'Lumen Financial Services' (via GroupM/Mindshare)**
Deal: PMG-IO-2026-0087 (Streaming) + PMG-IO-2026-0088 (Display/Programmatic) | Combined value: $520K | Negotiated term: 'Consolidated household frequency cap of 5x/day across all Prism properties including streaming and display.' | Deal owner: Angela Torres | Note (Jan 15, 2026): 'Client specifically called out cross-platform dedup as a requirement. Confirmed with ad ops we can honor via LiveRamp identity spine.'

**Google Ad Manager — Order: 'Lumen_Financial_Q1_Streaming'**
Line items: 8 | Frequency cap: 5x/household/day | Delivered: 28.4M impressions | Unique HH reached: 4.2M | Avg freq: 3.1x | Platform: Prism+ (CTV/streaming) | Identity: LiveRamp HH graph

**Monday.com — Campaign Tracker: 'Lumen Display Q1'**
Platform: Prism Web + App (display) | Served via: PMP deal through The Trade Desk | Impressions: 19.1M | Frequency cap: 5x/user/day | Identity: cookie-based + probabilistic | Note from trafficker (Feb 8): 'TTD uses their own identity graph — no LiveRamp integration on this path. Cross-platform dedup not technically possible in real-time.'

**Amplitude — Prism+ App Engagement Dashboard**
Household overlap analysis (Q1 2026): 34% of Prism+ streaming HHs also active on Prism web/app properties. Estimated cross-platform undeduplicated exposure for Lumen campaign: avg 6.8x/HH/day for overlap segment.

**Mixpanel — Prism Web Analytics**
Lumen Financial display campaign: avg 3.4x frequency per cookie. Note: cookie match rate to HH graph = ~62%.

**Slack — #ad-ops (Apr 2, 2026, 4:55 PM)**
@tasha.w: just got off the phone with Mindshare. they ran their own measurement and are claiming we exceeded the 5x consolidated cap by 30%+ for a third of their audience. they want a credit.
@angela.t: shit. what does our data show?
@tasha.w: depends which tool you look at. amplitude shows 6.8x overlap for the 34% shared-audience segment. each platform individually is compliant. it's the cross-platform dedup that broke
@angela.t: did we ever actually confirm the LiveRamp spine could cover the display path?
@tasha.w: 🫠 the feb 8 note in monday says TTD doesn't integrate with liveramp on the pmp path. so... no
@angela.t: who signed off on the IO language promising consolidated cap?
@tasha.w: you did lol. but tbf the CRM note says 'confirmed with ad ops we can honor' — I don't remember that convo
@angela.t: 😬
[thread ends]
